Morning,

The tea arrived. The box is under the galley counter, behind the cereal,
not in the cleaning cupboard where the last one ended up.

Could people stop putting the chipped blue mugs in the discard tray? They
belong to two of the night crew and they know which ones they are. I have
put a small card by the shelf. We have plenty of plain white mugs for
visitors. If the little lamp by the window has moved, please put it back;
it is easier on the eyes when the corridor lights are dimmed.

Zoey
